OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775831159
OL,1,Vk4                               G4/19
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGTHREE HOSTAGES
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGRELEASED IN LEBANON
OL,5, Three Western hostages, released by
OL,6, the Abu Nidal group in Lebanon, are
OL,7, preparing to fly home.
OL,9,FFrench woman Jacqueline Valente, her
OL,10,FBelgian boyfriend Fernand Houtekins
OL,11,Fand their daughter Sophie-Liberte were
OL,12,Fhanded over to French diplomats.
OL,14,FThere is speculation they spent some of
OL,15,Ftheir two and a half years in captivity
OL,16,Fin Libya after they were seized from a
OL,17,Fyacht in the eastern Mediterranean.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FTheir release follows an appeal by
OL,20,Fthe Libyan leader Muammar Gadaffi to
OL,21,Fmark the month of Ramadan.
OL,22,D
OL,23,D]FFromG10-04-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775831159
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/19
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGFRENCH HOSTAGES "NO
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGPRECEDENT FOR UK"
OL,4,F
OL,5, The Foreign Office has welcomed the
OL,6, release of the last French hostages in
OL,7, Lebanon but has ruled out any deal with
OL,8, hostage-takers over British hostages.
OL,10,FIn anticipation of renewed calls for
OL,11,Fmore flexibility in working for their
OL,12,Ffreedom, the FO said Foreign Secretary
OL,13,FDouglas Hurd would make every effort.
OL,15,FBut officials added that Britain
OL,16,Fremained convinced that deals only
OL,17,Fincreased the danger of further hostage
OL,18,Ftaking in the future.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FMeanwhile, efforts are continuing to
OL,21,Ffree four Belgians still held hostage.
OL,23,D]FFromG10-04-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
